Sometimes it is useful to process spawned process stdout and stderr in some way before out this to console. The current implementation of superspawn doesn't give a way to do this. One of the cases when this could be helpful - CB-9971 (see for some discussion).
The proposed approach is:
1. Add ability to accept any valid stdio configuration, just like the original child_process.spawn does (
2. Give a way to caller to listen to stdout and stderr events. This might be implemented as resultant promise progress notification:
{code:JavaScript}
spawn('mycommand', [], {stdio: 'pipe'})
.progress(function (stdio){
 if (stdio.stderr) {
 console.error(stdio.stderr);
 }
})
.then(function(result){
 // do other stuff
})
{code}
Another option is to return na object that implements both EventEmitter and Promise interfaces, so anybody might subscribe to its events.

